### Manual API walkthrough for IntelliJ HTTP Client (contains NO secrets).
### Run the requests top to bottom while the app is running on localhost:8080.

### 1. Register a user (unique email each run)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Ankit","email":"ankit{{$timestamp}}@example.com","password":"SecurePassword123"}

> {% client.global.set("userId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Create a savings account for that user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId":"{{userId}}","accountType":"SAVINGS"}

> {% client.global.set("accountId", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Deposit 1000.00  -> 201, balanceAfter 1000.00
POST http://localhost:8080/api/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposit
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":1000.00,"description":"initial deposit"}

### 4. Withdraw 300.00  -> 201, balanceAfter 700.00
POST http://localhost:8080/api/accounts/{{accountId}}/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":300.00,"description":"rent"}

### 5. Withdraw too much  -> 422 Insufficient funds
POST http://localhost:8080/api/accounts/{{accountId}}/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":5000.00}

### 6. Invalid amount  -> 400 with fieldErrors.amount
POST http://localhost:8080/api/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposit
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":-10}

### 7. Unknown account  -> 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/accounts/000000000000000000000000/deposit
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":10.00}

### 8. Check the balance  -> 700.00
GET http://localhost:8080/api/accounts/{{accountId}}